{
  "$comment": "Probe map for the Derma Intel v3 reference atlas. Coordinates are FRACTIONS of image width/height so the map survives any resize. mode: avg (whole-patch mean, for flat surfaces and gradient bands) | minluma (mean of the darkest 12%, for text strokes) | maxchroma (mean of the top 12% by chroma, for tiny vivid pills and dots). r = patch radius in px. white = the probe used as this image's white anchor for calibration (null = report raw only). expect = neutral | chromatic | dark, used by the sampler to flag probes that missed their target. Gradient probes deliberately WALK A DIAGONAL so the output is a ramp, not a colour.",
